x86_64-linux  The C1 forms of `Box<int>` and `Box<double>`'s constructor, and nothing else: `_ZNR3BoxIiE3getEv`, `_ZNO3BoxIiE3getEv`, `_ZNO3BoxIiE2asIiEEiv` and the rest agree with clang letter for letter, and the other two targets agree name for name. clang emits only the base-object C2 form of a class template's constructor on this target and calls it directly, where cxx1 emits the complete-object C1 beside it - the difference polymorphic-class-template.nonames and template-member.nonames record; this constructor is already out of line, and a class template's constructor is one clang still treats as inline there.
